<H1>Medium data</H1>
Search for medium no. = [902].
<HR>
Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121&#176;C for 15 min.
<HR>
<P><B><FONT SIZE=3>902&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;MJ MEDIUM FOR MICROAEROPHILIC AUTOTROPHS</FONT></B></P>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> MJ(-N) synthetic seawater (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=268">268</a>)       </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> L  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> NH<sub>4</sub>Cl                                                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.25&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components, adjust pH to 5.5 and autoclave.  After cooling, add aseptically the following solutions (filter-sterilized):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 8% NaHCO<sub>3</sub> solution                                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 10% Na<sub>2</sub>S<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>&#183;5H<sub>2</sub>O solution              </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;15.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace vitamins (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=197">197</a>)                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Distribute the medium into sterile culture vessels under a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub>-O<sub>2</sub> (76:19:5, v/v) gas mixture and seal with butyl rubber stoppers. Pressurize the culture vessels to 50 kPa with the same gas mixture.       <br>
